Adding District in run 2 raised gradient boosting AUC by about 0.002 and left logistic regression unchanged. From run 2 to run 3, AUC with all variables fell by about 0.002 for both models. Run 3 changed several things at once (the preprocessing pipeline, the candidate variables, and the apparent loss of isTrafficViolation), so the change cannot be attributed to any one of them.

3. Selection stability
The per-method fold counts (the stability table) for this run are not in the outputs I was given; only the consensus lists in section 4 are. The second run's table has been removed so that the log does not mix runs. Add feature_selection_stability.csv from this run to rebuild it.
Thirteen variables are stable (selected by the consensus rule in at least 4 of 5 folds): StopDescription, SubjectAge, SubjectGender, VehicleYear, SubjectWeight, SubjectRace, Zip, night, hour, SubjectHeight, isDriver, SubjectHasPhotoID, District. Whether each was chosen in 4 or 5 folds is not available.
Three variables are chosen on the full training set but in fewer than 4 of 5 folds: VehicleStyle, SubjectHairColor and month. They are borderline.
District and Zip are both stable. StopDescription, new in this run, is stable too.
isLA, weekend, VehicleColor and SubjectEyeColor appear in neither list. isLA was selected in every fold in the second run.

